Description: guitar tablature and score viewer
 OxiGuitar opens Guitar Pro files (.gp, .gpx, .gp5, .gp4, .gp3) and
 shows them as standard notation and tablature in four layouts, with any
 set of tracks together. It edits and saves them, exports them to PDF,
 and plays them with the system's sound set or better ones the user adds
 (SoundFont and SFZ). No telemetry: it never uploads anything.
 .
 OxiGuitar opens and plays files only through plugins; the package
 oxiguitar-plugins-basic, which it depends on, holds those for Guitar Pro
 files and sound.

Package: oxiguitar-plugins-basic
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 fluid-soundfont-gm | musescore-general-soundfont-small,
Enhances:
 oxiguitar,
Description: Guitar Pro format, sound and audio plugins for OxiGuitar
 The plugins the OxiGuitar project writes and recommends: one for each
 Guitar Pro format (3, 4, 5, 6 and 7-8), so OxiGuitar can open those
 files; the SoundFont player, which plays the tracks with a General MIDI
 or SFZ sound set; and the ones that play its sound through PipeWire or
 ALSA. OxiGuitar finds these in /usr/lib/oxiguitar/plugins.
